<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The second-to-last inequality is readily obtained from <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{l_{n}(h,s,a)+\nu_{h}(s,a)}{l_{n}(h,s,a)+1}\leq\max(\nu_{h}(s,a),1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{l_{n}(h,s,a)+\nu_{h}(s,a)}{l_{n}(h,s,a)+1}\leq\max(\nu_{h}(s,a),1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\nu_{h}(s,a)}{l_{n}(h,s,a)+\nu_{h}(s,a)}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\nu_{h}(s,a)}{l_{n}(h,s,a)+\nu_{h}(s,a)}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last inequality is enforced by the lower bound on beta specified in the theorem. Hence, the inequality <a href="#A2.E5" title="In Proof B.5 ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Prior-Aligned Meta-RL: Thompson Sampling with Learned Priors and Guarantees in Finite-Horizon MDPs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> has been proved.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof B.6</span></span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Prior-Aligned Meta-RL: Thompson Sampling with Learned Priors and Guarantees in Finite-Horizon MDPs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider some history <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{M}^{n}\in\mathcal{M}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{M}^{n}\in\mathcal{M}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal policy in MDP <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},H,P,R,s_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A},H,P,R,s_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Prior-Aligned Meta-RL: Thompson Sampling with Learned Priors and Guarantees in Finite-Horizon MDPs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> conditioned on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> shows that with probability at least <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\mu^{*},1}(s_{1})\geq V_{\mu^{*},1}(s_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\mu^{*},1}(s_{1})\geq V_{\mu^{*},1}(s_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. When this occurs, we always have <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})\geq V_{*,1}(s_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})\geq V_{*,1}(s_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, since by definition <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimal under our algorithm.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reduction to bounding online prediction error.</span> For the purposes of analysis, we let <math id="A2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{w}</annotation></semantics></math> denote an imagined second sample drawn from the same distribution as <math id="A2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{w}(h,s,a)|\mathcal{H}_{n-1}\sim N(0,Var(w)(h,s,a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{w}(h,s,a)|\mathcal{H}_{n-1}\sim N(0,Var(w)(h,s,a))</annotation></semantics></math> under our algorithm. More formally, let <math id="A2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{M}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{M}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> whose value function <math id="A2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{V}_{h}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{V}_{h}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> is estimated by our algorithm under <math id="A2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{w}</annotation></semantics></math>. Conditioned on the history, <math id="A2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{M}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{M}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> has the same marginal distribution as <math id="A2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{M}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{M}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, but it is statistically independent of the policy <math id="A2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> selected by RLSVI.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.7</span></span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For an absolute constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\Phi(-1)^{-1}&lt;6.31" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>6.31</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\Phi(-1)^{-1}&lt;6.31</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Regret}(T,M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Regret</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Regret}(T,M)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(c+1)\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}|\widetilde{V}_{n,1}(s_{1})-V_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})|\right]+c\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}|\overline{V}_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})-V_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})|\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(c+1)\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}|\widetilde{V}_{n,1}(s_{1})-V_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})|\right]+c\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}|\overline{V}_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})-V_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})|\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+H\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(\widehat{M}^{n}\notin\mathcal{M}^{n})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+H\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(\widehat{M}^{n}\notin\mathcal{M}^{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Online prediction error bounds.</span> We complete the proof with concentration arguments. Set <math id="A2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{R}^{n}(h,s,a)=\widehat{R}_{h,s,a}^{n}-R_{h,s,a}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{R}^{n}(h,s,a)=\widehat{R}_{h,s,a}^{n}-R_{h,s,a}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{P}^{n}(h,s,a)=\widehat{P}_{h,s,a}^{n}-P_{h,s,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{P}^{n}(h,s,a)=\widehat{P}_{h,s,a}^{n}-P_{h,s,a}\in\mathbb{R}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the error in estimating the mean reward and transition vector corresponding to <math id="A2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h,s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h,s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>. The next result follows by bounding each term in Lemma 6. We focus our analysis on bounding <math id="A2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}|\widetilde{V}_{n,1}(s_{1})-V_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})|\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}|\widetilde{V}_{n,1}(s_{1})-V_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})|\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. The other term can be bounded in an identical manner, so we omit this analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.8</span></span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\Phi(-1)^{-1}&lt;6.31" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>6.31</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\Phi(-1)^{-1}&lt;6.31</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}|\widetilde{V}_{n,1}(s_{1})-V_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})|\right]\leq\sqrt{\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{h=1}^{H-1}||\epsilon_{P}^{n}(h,s_{nh},a_{nh})||_{1}^{2}\right]}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{h=1}^{H-1}||\widetilde{V}_{n,h+1}||_{\infty}^{2}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}|\widetilde{V}_{n,1}(s_{1})-V_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})|\right]\leq\sqrt{\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{h=1}^{H-1}||\epsilon_{P}^{n}(h,s_{nh},a_{nh})||_{1}^{2}\right]}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{h=1}^{H-1}||\widetilde{V}_{n,h+1}||_{\infty}^{2}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{h=1}^{H}|\epsilon_{R}^{n}(h,s_{nh},a_{nh})|\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{h=1}^{H}|w^{n}(h,s_{nh},a_{nh})|\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\frac{\overline{\nu}}{l_{n}(h,s_{h},a_{h})+\overline{\nu}}H\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{h=1}^{H}|\epsilon_{R}^{n}(h,s_{nh},a_{nh})|\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{h=1}^{H}|w^{n}(h,s_{nh},a_{nh})|\right]+\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\frac{\overline{\nu}}{l_{n}(h,s_{h},a_{h})+\overline{\nu}}H\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The remaining lemmas complete the proof. At each stage, RLSVI adds Gaussian noise with standard deviation no larger than <math id="A2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(H^{3/2}\sqrt{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(H^{3/2}\sqrt{S})</annotation></semantics></math>. Ignoring extremely low probability events, we expect,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widetilde{V}_{n,h+1}\|_{\infty}\leq\widetilde{O}(H^{5/2}\sqrt{S})\text{ and hence }\sum_{h=1}^{H-1}\|\widetilde{V}_{n,h+1}\|_{\infty}^{2}\leq\widetilde{O}(H^{6}S)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and hence </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widetilde{V}_{n,h+1}\|_{\infty}\leq\widetilde{O}(H^{5/2}\sqrt{S})\text{ and hence }\sum_{h=1}^{H-1}\|\widetilde{V}_{n,h+1}\|_{\infty}^{2}\leq\widetilde{O}(H^{6}S).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p11.2" class="ltx_p">The proof of this Lemma makes this precise by applying appropriate maximal inequalities.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof B.9</span></span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8 ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Prior-Aligned Meta-RL: Thompson Sampling with Learned Priors and Guarantees in Finite-Horizon MDPs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>
We bound each term in the bound in Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8 ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Prior-Aligned Meta-RL: Thompson Sampling with Learned Priors and Guarantees in Finite-Horizon MDPs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>. By applying Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2 ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Prior-Aligned Meta-RL: Thompson Sampling with Learned Priors and Guarantees in Finite-Horizon MDPs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> with a choice of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{M}=M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{M}=M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{M}=\widetilde{M}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{M}=\widetilde{M}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the largest term is bounded, for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and reference to the proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Prior-Aligned Meta-RL: Thompson Sampling with Learned Priors and Guarantees in Finite-Horizon MDPs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\widetilde{V}_{n,1}(s_{1})-V_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\widetilde{V}_{n,1}(s_{1})-V_{\mu^{n},1}(s_{1})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}|w^{n}(h,s_{nh},a_{nh})|\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}|w^{n}(h,s_{nh},a_{nh})|\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
